From 1280f12399693e9cd40231042e4dc635a752b0b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: spotUP <retroranksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 22:04:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] socket: include <sys/uio.h> on AmigaOS as on OpenBSD

ixemul's <sys/socket.h> (4.4BSD) uses struct iovec without defining it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Modules/socketmodule.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Modules/socketmodule.c b/Modules/socketmodule.c
index f297a5f..f5ffff1 100644
--- a/Modules/socketmodule.c
+++ b/Modules/socketmodule.c
@@ -177,7 +177,7 @@ shutdown(how) -- shut down traffic in one or both directions\n\
 # undef HAVE_GETHOSTBYNAME_R_6_ARG
 #endif
 
-#if defined(__OpenBSD__)
+#if defined(__OpenBSD__) || defined(__amigaos__)
 # include <sys/uio.h>
 #endif
 
